1. What does BrowserRouter do?
2. Routes vs Route component
Route has path and element.
 <Route path="/about" element={<About />} />
3. Link - its usage
Link has to attribute. <Link to="/about">About</Link>
4. Handling path params using useParam
5. what is nested route - when you want to keep displaying some common ui on the page but changes some part of the page
6. Layout route - The layout routes does not have its path per say. It is used to create the layout for your website.
7. When we nest routes inside a parent route, react router is going to notice that this parent route does not havea  path so its going to match whatever path/url we are currently at and its going to rendre the Layout component and when it renders our layout component , we use <Outlet /> component to act like the placeholder to render the element of the child components.
<BrowserRouter>
      <Routes>
        <Route element={<Layout />}>
          <Route path="/" element={<Home />} />
          <Route path="/about" element={<About />} />
          <Route path="/vans" element={<Vans />} />
          <Route path="/vans/:id" element={<VanDetail />} />
        </Route>
      </Routes>
    </BrowserRouter>
  )
